wetterzentrale changes on top of NOAA-EMC/wgrib2
================================================

This fork (branch `wz`) is the upstream release v3.8.0 plus a few changes.
Upstream releases are merged into `wz` (see "Upgrading" below).

Changes
-------
1. extra/Mysql_speed_ens.c: new function `-mysql_speed_ens`, registered in
   extra/fnlist_extra.h, wgrib2/fnlist.c and wgrib2/fnlist.h. It is the
   ensemble variant of `-mysql_speed`:
   - the ensemble member comes from perturbation_number(); for centre 78
     (DWD ICON) one is subtracted because ICON has no control run;
   - the parameter mapping comes from the table
     `wgrib2_parameter_mapping_ens` (instead of `wgrib2_parameter_mapping`);
   - the column names get a member suffix, `<param>_<level>_P<nn>`;
   - the run time column `rt` is not loaded;
   - the limits are larger (MAX_NXNY 20,000,000; MAX_SQL_INSERT 30,000).
2. cmake/FindMySQL.cmake and extra/CMakeLists.txt: find and link the MySQL /
   MariaDB client library when USE_MYSQL=ON (the upstream CMake build only
   defines USE_MYSQL).
3. extra/fnlist_extra.h, wgrib2/fnlist.h: declare f_lev() and give the mysql
   functions their ARG5/ARG7 prototypes. Without this the build fails with
   GCC 14 and later (implicit declaration / incompatible pointer types).

Building
--------
The program is built as a conda package from the recipe in `recipe/` (the source of the build is a git tag of
this repository, set by `git_rev` in `recipe/meta.yaml`):

  cd recipe
  conda build . -c conda-forge --override-channels
  mamba install -n dwd314 -c <conda-bld channel> -c conda-forge --override-channels wgrib2=3.8.0=wz1_100

`recipe/build.sh` shows the CMake options (BUILD_EXTRA=ON, USE_MYSQL, USE_IPOLATES, USE_NETCDF, ...).
`recipe/conda_build_config.yaml` pins the compilers to gcc/gfortran 16 (nceplibs-ip's Fortran module files
need the same gfortran version). The MySQL client is mariadb-connector-c, which looks for the server
socket in /tmp/mysql.sock; use `socket=` in the [wgrib2] option file group or MYSQL_UNIX_PORT.

Not included compared with the old v3.1.3 build: Proj4 geolocation.

Upgrading
---------
  git fetch upstream --tags
  git checkout wz
  git merge vX.Y.Z

Conflicts can only be in wgrib2/fnlist.c, wgrib2/fnlist.h (in newer upstream
versions src/fnlist.*), extra/CMakeLists.txt and extra/fnlist_extra.h. After
a merge rebuild and compare the output with the previous binary.
